---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Terms of Service — ValoArt" description="ValoArt Terms of Service — how you may use the site, its arts, and its generators." active="">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </div>

  <section class="legal">
    <p>
      By using ValoArt, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please
      do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>What ValoArt provides</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt provides Valorant chat ASCII arts to browse and copy, a Text Gen
      tool to turn phrases into block-letter banners, and a Canvas tool to
      paint your own chat art. All of these are provided for personal use in
      VALORANT chat and similar chat contexts.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree to use ValoArt and its arts responsibly, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use arts to harass, threaten, or abuse other players.</li>
      <li>
        Do not use the site to break VALORANT's rules, Riot Games' terms, or
        any applicable law.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not attempt to disrupt the site, its analytics, or its copy-count
        service — for example, by artificially inflating copy counts.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not present ValoArt, or arts from ValoArt, as official Riot Games
        content.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may remove arts, change features, or restrict access at any time if
      use of the site breaks these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Arts and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Gallery arts are provided as-is for personal, non-commercial use in chat.
      Some arts are based on public fan art and community designs. If you own
      an art in the gallery and would like it removed, please contact us via
      the ValoArt GitHub repository at github.com/muse-codez/valoart, or via
      ruvix.lol, and we will review the request.
    </p>
    <p>
      Arts you create with Text Gen or Canvas are yours to use and share. By
      publishing a Canvas art on ValoArt, you agree that it may be shown to
      other visitors in that session, as described on the Canvas page.
    </p>
    <p>
      ValoArt's own branding, layout, and code remain the property of their
      respective owners. You may not copy the site itself and present it as
      your own.
    </p>

    <h2>Not affiliated with Riot Games</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt is a fan project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
      sponsored by, or connected to Riot Games, Inc. VALORANT and related
      names and marks are trademarks of Riot Games, Inc. Your use of arts in
      VALORANT chat is subject to Riot Games' own terms and rules.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt is provided “as is”, without warranties of any kind. We do not
      guarantee that arts will always paste correctly in every chat, that
      copy counts will always be accurate, or that the site will always be
      available without interruption.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, ValoArt and its operators are
      not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the site,
      its arts, or its tools, including any action taken against your game
      account for how you use arts in chat. You are responsible for how you
      use arts in VALORANT and for following Riot Games' rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date
      at the top will change when we do, and continued use of the site after
      a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about these terms, please open an issue on the
      ValoArt GitHub repository at github.com/muse-codez/valoart, or contact
      us via ruvix.lol.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .legal { padding: 0 0 80px; max-width: 760px; }
    .legal h2 {
      font-family: 'Outfit', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 24px;
      margin: 32px 0 10px;
    }
    .legal p, .legal li {
      font-family: 'Figtree', system-ui, sans-serif;
      color: #d8dde2;
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .legal ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
